{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2179-06-16 11:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. Johnson. I'm Dr. Patel, one of your transplant team doctors. I understand you came in because your liver tests were high and you’ve been having some tremors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2179-06-16 11:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. My wife noticed my hands shaking more than usual yesterday. And I’ve had some headaches too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2179-06-16 11:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You mentioned the tremors have been going on for a few weeks, but got worse recently?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2179-06-16 11:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, subtle at first—just a little shaky when I ate. But yesterday, my head started moving too, and I had trouble finding words for a moment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2179-06-16 11:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That sounds concerning. We’ll need to check a few things. You’re here for a liver biopsy today, which was planned because of the elevated liver enzymes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2179-06-16 11:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right. They marked my side earlier this morning. Is it safe? I’m a bit nervous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2179-06-16 11:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a routine procedure. We use imaging to guide the needle, and we’ll monitor your blood afterward to make sure there’s no bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2179-06-16 11:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. My appetite’s been poor lately. And the feeding tube got clogged a couple nights ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2179-06-16 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see that in your chart. We’ll keep an eye on your nutrition. For now, we’ll hold off on tube feeds since you’re able to eat a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2179-06-16 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The biopsy went well. No complications. We’ll get the results in a day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2179-06-16 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, doctor. I’ve been feeling a bit weak. Is that normal after the biopsy?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2179-06-16 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Some fatigue is expected. We’ll keep you lying on your side for a few hours to reduce any risk of bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2179-06-16 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked a chest X-ray to make sure your PICC line is in the right place. It is—good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2179-06-16 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s one less thing to worry about. What about the tremors? Could they be from the transplant meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2179-06-16 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Tacrolimus can cause tremors, but the new movements you’re describing—head shaking, facial grimacing—make us want to look further."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2179-06-16 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s next?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2179-06-16 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve ordered an MRI of your head and cervical spine to rule out any structural issues. Given your pain, we may not be able to do the full study, but we’ll try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2179-06-16 21:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The head MRI is back. No stroke or bleeding. But there’s some chronic small vessel disease and brain atrophy—common with age and your history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2179-06-16 21:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that why I’m having tremors?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2179-06-16 21:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not likely. Those changes don’t explain the sudden movements. The cervical MRI showed arthritis in your neck, but no spinal cord compression."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2179-06-16 21:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s causing it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2179-06-16 21:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re not sure yet. A neurologist is reviewing your case. We’re also checking your potassium—it was high earlier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2179-06-16 21:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "High potassium? I didn’t know that could affect movement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2179-06-16 21:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can cause muscle weakness or irregular heartbeats, but not typically tremors. Still, we’re treating it with medication to bring it down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2179-06-17 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The liver ultrasound shows no bile duct blockage, but we’re still concerned. We’re scheduling an ERCP to look directly at the bile ducts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2179-06-17 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Another procedure? What’s an ERCP?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2179-06-17 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a scope passed through your mouth to the liver area. We can see the bile ducts and fix any narrow spots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2179-06-17 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be asleep?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2179-06-17 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll be sedated. We’ll remove the feeding tube temporarily for the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2179-06-17 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The ERCP went well. We found a narrow spot at the bile duct connection. We opened it and placed two stents to keep it open."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2179-06-17 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2179-06-17 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. This should help your liver numbers improve. Your enzymes are already trending down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2179-06-17 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the tremors?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2179-06-17 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’ve improved since yesterday. The neurologist thinks they may not be from a physical cause. Stress or anxiety could be playing a role."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2179-06-17 13:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been stressed, sure. But it felt real."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2179-06-17 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was real. But sometimes the body expresses emotional strain through physical symptoms. We’ve involved social work to help with family stress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2179-06-18 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your potassium is still high. We’ve started Florinef and low-dose Lasix to help your kidneys manage it better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2179-06-18 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need these long-term?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2179-06-18 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll see. It may improve as your liver function stabilizes. We’ll monitor closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2179-06-19 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been having right upper belly pain with eating. We did an EGD—just mild stomach irritation, nothing serious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2179-06-19 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So why does it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2179-06-19 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly from bile flow changes or your hiatal hernia. We’ve switched you to a stronger stomach protector—lansoprazole."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2179-06-20 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your tremors haven’t returned. That’s a good sign. The neuro team feels it’s safe to cancel the lumbar MRI."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2179-06-20 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I couldn’t have stayed still anyway—my back hurts too much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2179-06-20 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We don’t want to put you through unnecessary pain. Your liver tests are improving thanks to the stents."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2179-06-21 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked another scan to make sure the stents haven’t moved. They’re in place—great news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2179-06-21 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m healing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2179-06-21 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Your liver numbers are going down, potassium is better, and you’re eating well. We’re thinking about discharge soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2179-06-22 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The transplant team evaluated you. You’re stable and safe to go home. We’ll set up visiting nurses and labs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2179-06-22 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll need help with meds, though. My wife and daughter can assist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2179-06-22 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do a full med teaching session. You’re on tacrolimus, prednisone, and insulin—same as before, with a few changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2179-06-22 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like what?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2179-06-22 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll start ursodiol for bile flow, mirtazapine for sleep and appetite, and fludrocortisone for potassium control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2179-06-22 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the tremors—what if they come back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2179-06-22 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call us immediately if you have dizziness, confusion, or shaking. But we’re hopeful it won’t return."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today’s the day. You’re doing well—walking on your own, eating, and stable vitals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Remember: labs tomorrow, then weekly. Take your meds as shown, and call if you feel worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And thank the nurses too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’ll pass that along. Take care, Mr. Johnson. We’ll see you in clinic soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing—should I avoid lifting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, nothing over 10 pounds for now. And no driving until your next appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set. The discharge papers are ready, and your family can bring the car around."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad this is behind me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve made great progress. Keep following up, and take it one day at a time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. Johnson."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last question—what about my headaches?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’re likely tension-type, related to stress. The mirtazapine should help with sleep and reduce them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll give it a try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good plan. And keep using the antacid as needed for stomach discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set. We’ll be in touch after your first lab results."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, doctor. Really appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care of yourself and keep in touch."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye, Mr. Johnson."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will help you get ready to leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2179-06-23 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2179-06-16 11:22:00",
    "admission_end": "2179-06-23 21:55:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A male patient, status post orthotopic liver transplant, was admitted for evaluation of elevated liver enzymes and new-onset tremors. A liver biopsy was performed, which ruled out rejection but showed neutrophilic inflammation. An ERCP revealed a biliary stricture at the anastomosis, which was treated with sphincterotomy and placement of two biliary stents. His liver function tests subsequently improved. He developed hyperkalemia, managed with kayexalate, fludrocortisone, and low-dose furosemide. Neurological evaluation for abnormal involuntary movements, including head shaking and facial grimacing, found no acute intracranial or spinal cord abnormalities on MRI; the movements resolved, and a psychological component was considered. An EGD showed only mild gastropathy. The patient stabilized, resumed oral intake, and was discharged home with family support, visiting nurse services, and a plan for weekly lab monitoring.",
    "problems": [
      "Complications of transplanted liver",
      "Obstruction of bile duct",
      "Hyperpotassemia",
      "Abnormal involuntary movements",
      "Abdominal pain, right upper quadrant",
      "Migraine, unspecified, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus",
      "Other specified disorders of stomach and duodenum",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Insomnia, unspecified",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of prostate"
    ]
  }
}
